Z||000029||JSocha||06-12-2001||10:31 AM||||Sorry, dog lover here (owner of 7 dogs...3 Tea cup Poodles, 1 not sure if it is a Poodle/Terrier cross, 2 American Eskimos and a Collie).  I never have liked cats since I was little.  Something about them slinking around my legs or next to me that bugs the h3ll out of me.<P>Anyways, how bout "$h*thead"?  There heads are always in their butt area anyways, so I think it would be appropriate.  And here they call cats "Conosouirs!"  What Consoure do you know that licks their butt's? (Gallagher)<P>We call one of our female American Eskimos "Butt Heads" (real name is Buttons) and our Collie (Lady), "$h*t-for-Brains".  <P>The estimated Poodle/Terrier cross (Precious) I call "Lard @$$", even though she only weighs two pounds.  Snuggles (other American Eskimo) "Butt Wipe"; Buffy, "Buffer Wuffers"; Baby (10 yr old), Dumpling; Baby (new 3yr), "Dummy".<P>Now for the cats in the barn:  <BR>Cat<BR>Lucky (cause I haven't killed the b@st@rd yet.  But next time he lands on top of my head or my shoulders with his claws dug in, his 9th life should finally be up)<BR>Moving Target<BR>Bullseye and <BR>W.T.F. (you all know what the abbrev stands for, because there is no explaining what it is!  Thinks its a horse one time, bucking like a horse out in the pasture and eating oats.  Has to have its oats; and the next time it thinks its a dog...this little SOB doesn't meow, but tries to BARK!  I $h*t you not my fellow Fiero Brothers!).<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
